  "purpose": "MATVEC body clock-structure closure as LANDED REGIONS (landed-regions-standard-1018); not attention/fullSM/native chip qualification.",
  "structural_change": "rp4lp (PL-SMT 10-18, landed-regions-standard-1018): rp4m ran ONE balanced spine over 457.92 x 1529.28 um (TT insertion 1.53 ns, child-flop boundary ~91 ps). Now 2 clock regions from tools/landed_parent/lp.py (spec results/arch/landed_parent_1018/pl_smt/rp4_lp_spec.json): n = leaf 0 + row 0 + the whole bin beat path (pin flops, beat_t, pte beat, land_n) + N gather relays; s = leaf 1 + row 1 + land_s + S-edge gather outputs. Minimum-crossing cut (bin is broadcast to land_n, beat_t and land_s): 3 landings (bin_l->land_s 2,069 b, leaf-0 gather 50 b, pass gather 100 b; ring D4/E=K=2, +3 edges), pads 3 x (818 + 26) b in front of leaf 1, reset runs depth 3 replace the 5-stage u_rt tree. Ports: kit top = lp output ot_hbm_smh_rp4_flat_lp (rin / rout split per region: rin_n / rout_n = old 817:0, rin_s / rout_s = old 1635:818), clk -> ck_n + ck_s; offsets gout +3, all others 0. PL-KIT landed-cluster clock (multiple_cts_roots per region, landed_record) replaces the gate-1 spine form, whose S-root IO latency mismatch gave FF hold -957 ps on 1,282 S-region input endpoints. Outline h 1529.28 -> 1598.4 (GEN2 SM frame row): N half +69.12. Same 18 CLOSED child views.",
  "extra_paths": [
